      {
        "review_id": 902743195,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r902743195-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Special visit",
        "text": "During volunteering in Nepal the volunteer organisation planned some tours of  many of the main tourist attractions and heritage sites in Kathmandu.\n\nDuring the visit, the guide was very well informed and lived at the site in a cave directly beneath the temple. \n\nWhen arriving at the temple, there were massive crowds and we were told that the prime ministers’ wife had passed away and her funeral service (cremation) was happening at the temple with many police, army officers and officials present including the prime minister.\n\nWe toured the temple courtyard and sat in front of the cremation area for the prime ministers wife. Our guide talked us through the temple and the ceremonies. We then had the opportunity to meet the prime minster and then went to our guides cave. We didn’t enter the temple as it wasn’t open and it only allows Hindus inside. It costs 1,000 NP to enter. I’d suggest organising a guide and politely saying no to those selling things in the area.\n\nWe visited during a very important event, so it was very crowded, but would assume this would be different during normal times. It’s a very sacred place and linked to Shiva and the Hindu Gods. Definitely worth a visit but I would recommend being respectful as it is a location where people celebrate their dead and cremate their family.",
