        "title": "Extremely Disappointing",
        "text": "I am teaching in Kathmandu for several weeks, and was excited to visit this temple today. We were happy to pay the 15.00 USD to support this historic sight. Perhaps it is my fault for not doing enough research-- but to discover we were not allowed (as non-Hindus) into the temple courtyard was extremely disappointing. (It was our understanding that we could enter the courtyard, just not the temple.) There is not a lot more to see that we could not see at many other historic temples in India and Nepal without the expense. The cremation grounds are interesting (keeping a respectful distance)- but admission is not necessary to see those. Just want to make it very clear- you will not be able to see much for the price that you will pay.",
