      {
        "review_id": 878399108,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r878399108-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Really disappointing and felt unsafe",
        "text": "We were really disappointed by this temple. Whilst it was strangely fascinating to see bodies being cremated it wasn’t worth the entry fee (Rs 1000) which we thought we very expensive considering prices in Nepal. \n\nIt was a 30 minute taxi journey from Thamel to the temple. As soon as we got out the taxi, we were hounded by men saying hello, trying to sell things and asking for photos which continued along the walk to the temple and in the walls itself. It was the only place in Nepal we felt unsafe (collectively we have travelled to the majority of Asian countries) due to being three female travellers in our 20s. \n\nThe temple grounds were littered with rubbish and sadly had multiple people begging. There was also a constant hounding from workers offering a tour which we didn’t want. When ascending the steps there are multiple temples and shrines but felt unable to explore them due to the monkeys and men. \n\nPerhaps without feeling unsafe it would have been more enjoyable but compared to other sites in Kathmandu, it was disappointing with an expensive entry ticket.",
