        "title": "Hindu temple cremation ceremony...",
        "text": "The visit to this temple was both moving and thought provoking...a guide took me around and explained that the body after death was cremated on the same day according to the religious practice...\n\nThe body is washed and wrapped in a white cloth and all the family are involved in the cremation ceremony which is not a sad event but a celebration of the life...\n\nWhen the body is prepared for the cremation a taper is placed into the mouth and a male member of the family light up the taper!\n\nAn experience I shall never forget...",
